"description": "The catalogue browser, as a shot: a search box that types its query, filter chips with a count, and a grid of cards that rise in, each holding a LIVE render of a real atom (give the atom block as the card's preview) with its name, description, surface badge and source. One card can be picked: it lifts and takes an accent outline as step goes 0 to 1. p 0 to 0.3 types the query, p 0.3 to 1 brings the cards in. Use it to show a library of components honestly, with real names, real descriptions and real renders, instead of a mock-up. Plain HTML and CSS, no script; standalone it renders the finished screen.",
